The following test files in Cassandra's
test/unit/org/apache/cassandra/cql3/functions directory, which this
directory mirrors, were not translated, because they test Cassandra's
internal implementation through Java APIs instead of testing CQL:

* ClusterMetadataFctsTest.java: calls Cassandra's internal function for
  the kind of a cluster metadata transformation (part of Cassandra's
  transactional cluster metadata, TCM) directly, through Java.
* MathFctsTest.java: calls the implementations of the abs(), exp(), log(),
  log10() and round() functions directly, through Java, on Cassandra's
  internal type classes.
* NativeFunctionsTest.java: checks Cassandra's internal list of native
  functions, that each function with an old camelCase name has a new
  snake_case name, through Cassandra's internal function registry. Scylla's
  lack of snake_case names is SCYLLADB-5141.
* TimeFctsTest.java: calls the implementations of the time functions
  (mintimeuuid(), maxtimeuuid(), totimestamp(), tounixtimestamp(), etc.)
  directly, through Java. These functions are tested through CQL in
  validation/entities/timeuuid_test.py and in test_native_functions.py.

Note also that in function_factory_test.py, most of the tests of
FunctionFactoryTest.java were not translated - see the comment at the top
of that file - and that the masking/ subdirectory is empty - see its README.
